  "task": {
    "objective": "Carry each settlement's finite shipment to its assigned market, using fuel, temporary crossing reservations, escorts and dated signals to manage the single mountain pass.",
    "natural_termination": "Natural completion when all three original shipments are delivered; otherwise truncate at tick 150.",
    "interaction": "A reservation delays competing entry; relinquishing it enables others. An escort spends one actor's fuel/action to protect another caravan against closed-pass entry. Relay fuel buys a delayed observation for remote peers; simultaneous entry contests block all contenders.",
    "observation_access": "Public information is the map, settlement/market locations, clock/terminal causes, council reservation/lease and market receipts. Agents, their visible fuel/guard/stock/load, beacons and cargo are observed only within Manhattan radius two. Current pass weather is shown only within radius two of its physical position. Each actor additionally receives its own report and original timestamp. Beacon payloads and timestamps are local; pending packets are never observed. Visibility masks suppress all hidden record data to -1. Legal movement does not reveal hidden actors; weather/lease entry checks only occur when the acting caravan is already adjacent to the pass and can directly see it."
  },
